{"_v":3,"id":"the-maids-west-end-2025","cat":"off-west-end","cs":63.06,"rc":11,"bd":{"rave":1,"positive":3,"mixed":4,"negative":3},"rv":[{"cn":"Sam Marlowe","o":"The Stage","s":100,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://www.thestage.co.uk/reviews/the-maids-review-donmar-warehouse-london","d":"2025-10-22","q":"It’s draining, it’s overwhelming, it’s kind of gross – and it’s brilliant.","or":"5/5 stars"},{"cn":"Arifa Akbar","o":"The Guardian","s":82,"b":"Positive","t":1,"v":"positive","u":"https://www.theguardian.com/stage/2025/oct/22/the-maids-review-dorian-gray-kip-williams-donmar-warehouse-jean-genet","d":"2025-10-22","q":"It is draining, discomfiting, exhilarating.","or":"4/5 stars"},{"cn":"Nick Curtis","o":"Evening Standard","s":80,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://www.standard.co.uk/culture/theatre/the-maids-at-donmar-warehouse-review-b1254221.html","d":"2025-10-22","q":"But if you’re prepared to surrender, it’s a wild ride.","or":"4/5 stars"},{"cn":"Sarah Hemming","o":"Financial Times","s":60,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://www.ft.com/content/a95b7760-5960-4129-8ffe-77291b200cb8","d":"2025-10-22","q":"But the show begins to feel trapped by its own approach.","or":"3/5 stars"},{"cn":"Clive Davis","o":"The Times (UK)","s":60,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://www.thetimes.com/culture/theatre-dance/article/the-maids-review-katie-price-donmar-warehouse-93fqwlbb2","d":"2025-10-22","q":"The vibrant visuals leave you feeling as if you’ve been locked in a cupboard with Paris Hilton and Katie Price","or":"3/5 stars"},{"cn":"Andrzej Lukowski","o":"Time Out London","s":60,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://www.timeout.com/london/theatre/the-maids-6-review","d":"2025-10-21","q":"But for all its alluring digital dazzle, it leaves Williams’s production rather one note and exhausting.","or":"3/5 stars"},{"cn":"Alice Saville","o":"The Independent","s":40,"b":"Negative","t":1,"u":"https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/theatre-dance/reviews/the-maids-donmar-warehouse-kip-williams-b2849938.html","d":"2025-10-22","q":"Instead, it feels like spending one hour and forty minutes eavesdropping on private conversations that are so trivial you wish you hadn't bothered.","or":"2/5 stars"},{"cn":"Claire Allfree","o":"The Telegraph","s":40,"b":"Negative","t":1,"u":"https://www.telegraph.co.uk/theatre/what-to-see/the-maids-genet-donmar-warehouse/","d":"2025-10-22","q":"In Williams’s version, it’s borderline unwatchable.","or":"2/5 stars"},{"cn":"Stuart King","o":"London Box Office","s":70,"b":"Positive","t":2,"v":"positive","u":"https://www.londonboxoffice.co.uk/news/post/the-maids-donmar-warehouse-review","d":"2025-10-23","q":"Later, when joined by Madame (Yerin Ha), we are treated to a masterclass in erratic petulance, spite, entitlement and ego.","or":"3/5 stars"},{"cn":"Alex Wood","o":"WhatsOnStage","s":60,"b":"Mixed","t":2,"u":"https://www.whatsonstage.com/news/the-maids-at-donmar-warehouse-review_1699225/","d":"2025-10-22","q":"If The Maids never fully coheres, it nonetheless reaffirms Williams as one of the most distinctive directors working today.","or":"3/5 stars"},{"cn":"Stefan Kyriazis","o":"Express (UK)","s":12,"b":"Pan","t":3,"v":"negative","u":"https://www.express.co.uk/entertainment/theatre/2124334/maids-review-donmar-theatre","d":"2025-10-22","q":"This show is not. Avoid at all costs.","or":"1/5 stars"}],"cn":{"t":"Critics are split: one finds this high-speed, screen-heavy Genet adaptation an exhausting assault, while another praises its brash, eye-popping innovation from director Kip Williams.","rc":11},"pd":"2025-10-13","cov":{"state":"no-census-yet","liveCount":0,"candidateCount":0,"computedAt":"2026-11-21T12:21:28.060Z"}}